# Happiness Is a Warm Gun, second part, "I Need a Fix" (figure 136.3)
# An eleven-bar waltz phrase (3 + 4 + 4 bars), guitar and vocal shown separately as Pollack has
# them. He types each bar in beat columns, so the bunched groups are read by column: "E DCA" is E,
# D on beat 2, C on its off-beat, A on beat 3; "EDE" is E, D on the off-beat, E on beat 2 (held);
# "E G" is E and a held G; a lone "G" fills the bar.
# He types the chord in the last line as "c" but labels it III; it is drawn as C major, which the
# E-naturals in the tune over it confirm.
#? The chord typed "c" is drawn as C major (labelled III); check on the record.
#? Octaves: both lines are put around E4 (the vocal's register); the guitar may sound an octave lower.
